    "created_at": "2018-10-16T15:57:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-10-16T15:57:55Z",
    "body": "Had an offline discussion with @fserb. We agree it should be ready for vertical text, especially when we want to apply the same interface/semantics in Houdini.\r\n\r\nWe would like the bounding box to be logical, relative to the baseline, so what it should mean is \"line left\" and \"line right\" as you mentioned. We have mild preference to use \"Left\" and \"Right\" for the name as I think it's easier to understand. WDYT?\r\n\r\n`*Ascent` and `*Descent` should also be relative to the baseline, regardless of the orientation of the baseline. @litherum and I had early discussion on what kind of `*Ascent` and `*Descent` are needed, and as you know, currently these values are under defined. I'll open another issue for this.\r\n\r\n/cc @FremyCompany @r12a ",
